{
  "_note": "The workbench's options: hand-maintained from the ledgers (docs/superpowers/plans/*-ledger.md) and the workbench plan's Global Constraints. ids are app/song/library.h's (sym names the enum; smoke.mjs checks them); short: a bass instrument's name in the Bass part's own dropdown and header ('Electric'), its name elsewhere ('Electric bass'); a kit from 16 is a workbench preset (wb_drums.h's WB_KIT_*, 16 + its index). status: approved (offered, the dice pick it), candidate (offered, marked; the dice skip it; none among the instruments; a candidate comping style is one the roll weighs 0: none now), retired (behind 'show retired'), removed (a comping style never offered, not even behind 'show retired': light eighths, Sam 2026-11-05, its id 7 kept; an old snapshot's restores as held, said on restore). A comping style's keys: the keys instruments it plays on, only those; notKeys: never on these (the guitars only strum, Sam 2026-11-04). The Comping row lists every keys comping rhythm from one source, compRhythms (generated, below: Sam, 2026-11-05, \"I think of all comping rhythms the same\"), then strum and the retired styles (comping, here: only the styles that aren't rhythms; CS_PAT's entry is never offered itself, an old snapshot's comping 9, a rhythm drawn from the seed, shows as the current value only). ride: the kit plays the ride section (the sampled kits). set: a shipped sampled kit's sample set (samples/kits.json, git-ignored: unavailable until tools/prep_kits.py has made it). Families (Sam, 2026-10-29: the synth/acoustic divide applies to drums only): a song's family chooses its kit (the family row swaps the kit, its dice and the lanes' draw stay in the family; electric goes with either); the keys, bass, pad and lead mix freely across families. No ear candy (Sam, 2026-10-29): the instruments that only played it (the music box, the bells, none) have no role. The choir (the formant oo-aah, of any family): a pad a song may draw over its set's (library's lib_song_pad, 1 song in 4), and one of the pad's solo voices, in the vox pad's place (the vox pad retired, 2026-10-31: no patch). The organ is the tonewheel (2026-10-31; electric, as the Rhodes): on the keys the song's drawbars and register; as a pad (its one-stop 4', the scanner chorus by section) a song may draw it over its set's (lib_song_pad, about 1 song in 7, never over organ keys). Leads (Sam, 2026-10-29): the felt piano leads too (never over felt keys), the vibes are the vibraphone (sampled, then modeled from 2026-11-03), on the keys too from 2026-11-05 (the motor on; held, half notes, held on 2 (and 4), the comp rhythms; never with the vibes lead); the muted trumpet, sax, guitar lick, string lead and cello are retired; the lead instruments are the flute, felt piano, vibes and acoustic piano (lead styles build: the kalimba, saw lead and synth pluck retired, the electric guitar on the keys only). An old snapshot's retired lead plays the flute or the vibes in its place (library.c's lib_lead_approved), said on restore. Removed with their models (2026-10-31: no patch, so no role, not even behind 'show retired'): the upright (an old snapshot's bass plays the electric bass: lib_bass_approved, said on restore), the kalimba, saw lead and synth pluck, the music box and the bells; the Wurli and the DX electric piano (Sam, 2026-11-04: an old snapshot's keys play the Rhodes: lib_keys_approved, said on restore). Lead styles (lead styles, 2026-10-31): the lead_style override's values, 2 + leads.h's LS_*; the phrase planner (0) and the hybrid (1) are retired (an old snapshot naming one restores on a rolled style). Generated (tools/patterns/import.py, from patterns/; never edit them here): patterns (a new one named by its file), kickPhrases, strumPats and compRhythms (id: patterns/model.json's; index: the engine table's, which the override row forces). compRhythms: every keys comping rhythm in the engine's table order, with the keys its data names (keys, or notKeys: the guitars, which strum); value is the Comping row's (a fixed rhythm's CS_* id, staged as the COMP override; an added one's 100 + its index, its table index, the COMP_PAT override), so old snapshots restore as they were. A candidate there plays only when picked; Approve writes patterns/status.json, and tools/patterns/import.sh makes it one the roll draws.",
